    "title": "Ed Bentley named new head boys basketball coach at East Noble - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Josh Ayen ,\n1 hours ago\nKENDALLVILLE, Ind. (WANE) – A familiar face from the Highlight Zone is coming back to coach high school hoops at East Noble High School. Ed Bentley was approved to take over as head boys basketball coach during East Noble’s school board meeting on Wednesday.\nBentley has over a decade of experience as a head coach in northeast Indiana. He led Angola’s boys basketball program from 2012-20, leading the Hornets to three sectional championships in his tenure. Bentley also coached at Westview for the 2020-21 season before spending two seasons as Eastside’s head coach from 2021-23.\nFollowing his time at Eastside, Bentley joined Trine men’s basketball’s coaching staff as an assistant. Bentley was part of the coaching staff that helped the Thunder win a Div. III national championship in the 2023-24 season.\nBentley takes over for Brandon Durnell, whose employment was terminated during East Noble’s most recent school board meeting.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
